type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeDepthFirstSearchEvent"},{"text":"s, in the order ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DepthFirstSearch"},{"text":" reports them, with every edge","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"classified as a tree, back, forward or cross edge. Parallel edges are told apart: a repeated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree edge is a forward edge at its own position. It holds a copy of the graph and can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterated more than once. The search keeps its own stack, so a deep graph cannot overflow the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"call stack."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal\/EdgeDepthFirstSearch","title":"EdgeDepthFirstSearch"}}}